# Root .dockerignore.
#
# The api / migrate / seed / backfill images all build with the REPOSITORY ROOT as their
# context (see infra/docker-compose.yml `context: ..`), so without this every one of them
# uploads the whole tree. That became a real cost in PR-6, which installs the frontend's
# node_modules — hundreds of megabytes shipped to the daemon on every backend build.
#
# `web/.dockerignore` does not help: a .dockerignore only applies to the context ROOT.

# Frontend build output and dependencies
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/.vite

# Python artefacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
ml/artifacts

# VCS, editors, local env
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
.env
*.log

# Source data. NOTHING under data/ belongs in an image: `data/curated` is bind-mounted at
# runtime by the `api`, `seed` and `simulator` services, and `data/raw` is large and unused
# by any service. (The earlier version of this file excluded only `data/raw` while its own
# comment claimed curated was excluded too — so every backend build still shipped the real
# CSV to the daemon.)
data/

# Docs and design assets are not needed by any image.
docs
design
coding-logs
.codex
